  "content": {
    "title": "Bill Self details health scare, says he feels good after KU win at Colorado",
    "text": "Kansas men’s basketball coach Bill Self said he is feeling well and ready to return.Self shared new details Wednesday during his weekly radio show, Hawk Talk, one day after Kansas Jayhawks won at Colorado without him on the bench.“It is what it is,” Self said. “Right before our team was taking off, I started feeling some abnormal chest issues. I'm thinking, based on what I had before, it can't be good.”Self said doctors determined he was dehydrated and experiencing AFib, a heart rhythm issue he has dealt with previously.“I was experiencing some stuff,” he said. “I was not severely, but very dehydrated and I got AFib. I just had a bout with that, so that was pretty significant in a very small snippet of time, but it was enough that I couldn’t get on a plane.”Kansas officials said earlier this week that Self was taken to the hospital “out of an abundance of caution” and received IV fluids. “I've been checked out thoroughly. I actually feel good,” he said. “I'm good to go. I could coach today. I could have coached last night, but they didn't want me to fly.”Self previously underwent a heart procedure in 2023. LAWRENCE, Kan. —Kansas men’s basketball coach Bill Self said he is feeling well and ready to return.Self shared new details Wednesday during his weekly radio show, Hawk Talk, one day after Kansas Jayhawks won at Colorado without him on the bench. “It is what it is,” Self said. “Right before our team was taking off, I started feeling some abnormal chest issues. I'm thinking, based on what I had before, it can't be good.”Self said doctors determined he was dehydrated and experiencing AFib, a heart rhythm issue he has dealt with previously.“I was experiencing some stuff,” he said. “I was not severely, but very dehydrated and I got AFib. I just had a bout with that, so that was pretty significant in a very small snippet of time, but it was enough that I couldn’t get on a plane.”Kansas officials said earlier this week that Self was taken to the hospital “out of an abundance of caution” and received IV fluids. “I've been checked out thoroughly. I actually feel good,” he said. “I'm good to go. I could coach today. I could have coached last night, but they didn't want me to fly.” Self previously underwent a heart procedure in 2023.",
